        <mxCell id="c43" value="&lt;i&gt;Drawn to scale from zero. The sales-volume variance is 27 times the price gap and the discounts together, which add up to the flexible-budget variance (&lt;span style=&quot;white-space:nowrap&quot;&gt;−$1,281,870&lt;/span&gt;), so those two bars are slivers. The budget plans 3.5 times the units sold.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="464" width="860" height="38" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
